{"title":"Career Roadmap · Research Assistant","role":"Research Assistant","summary":"A Research Assistant (Psychology) supports research projects through literature reviews, participant recruitment, data collection, interviews, experiments, behavioural observation, data cleaning, statistical analysis, documentation, and research reporting.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BA (General / Honours) — Applied Psychology / Counselling / Neuropsychology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Research intern, psychology research assistant, project assistant, behavioural research intern"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Research Assistant/Associate in psychology, cognitive science, behavioural science or health research"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Research Associate, Study Coordinator, Research Manager or specialist researcher"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Senior Researcher, Principal Investigator, Research Programme Lead or academic/research specialist"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Research Assistant (Psychology) supports research projects through literature reviews, participant recruitment, data collection, interviews, experiments, behavioural observation, data cleaning, statistical analysis, documentation, and research reporting."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BA in Applied Psychology / Counselling / Neuropsychology, this is a strong entry pathway into psychological research, behavioural science, cognitive science, neuropsychology research, mental-health research, education research, UX research, health research, and academic research."},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"A Research Assistant is not automatically a psychologist, counsellor, clinical psychologist, or neuropsychologist. Those professions can require additional postgraduate qualifications, supervised training, registration/licensing, and jurisdiction-specific requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong alignment, particularly for psychology and behavioural research."},{"type":"p","text":"The most important addition to the BA is research methodology + statistics + data analysis + academic writing + research ethics."},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Psychology","Research Methods","Statistics","Experimental Design","Data Analysis","Academic Writing","Ethics","Digital/AI Research Tools"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Exact progression depends on qualifications, research output, institution and research area."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Psychology foundations"},{"text":"BA curriculum + research reading"},{"text":"Literature summary portfolio"},{"text":"Subject foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research methods"},{"text":"Research-methods coursework"},{"text":"Mini research proposal"},{"text":"Research"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Statistics + R/SPSS/Python"},{"text":"Statistical analysis report"},{"text":"Quantitative skills"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Experimental/behavioural research"},{"text":"Lab/field projects"},{"text":"Small study"},{"text":"Research execution"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Qualitative research + interviews"},{"text":"Qualitative-methods training"},{"text":"Interview/coding project"},{"text":"Mixed methods"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research internship"},{"text":"University/lab/research organisation"},{"text":"Internship + research output"},{"text":"Employability"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Psychology/neuroscience research"},{"text":"Research paper"},{"text":"Domain depth"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Dissertation + research portfolio"},{"text":"Faculty supervision"},{"text":"Dissertation + poster/paper"},{"text":"Research readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core psychology foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Build knowledge in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Personality"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Emotion"},{"text":"Biological psychology"},{"text":"Abnormal psychology"},{"text":"Health psychology"},{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Organisational psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a neuropsychology-oriented pathway, add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain anatomy"},{"text":"Neurobiology"},{"text":"Cognitive neuroscience"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Executive functions"},{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Perception"},{"text":"Neuropsychological assessment concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core employability skill for a Research Assistant."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Research question"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem","Literature","Gap","Research question","Hypothesis","Design","Data","Analysis","Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research designs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental"},{"text":"Quasi-experimental"},{"text":"Correlational"},{"text":"Cross-sectional"},{"text":"Longitudinal"},{"text":"Survey"},{"text":"Case study"},{"text":"Observational"},{"text":"Mixed methods"},{"text":"Qualitative research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Experimental concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Independent variable"},{"text":"Dependent variable"},{"text":"Control variable"},{"text":"Confound"},{"text":"Randomisation"},{"text":"Control group"},{"text":"Experimental group"},{"text":"Blinding"},{"text":"Replication"},{"text":"Internal validity"},{"text":"External validity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Remember:"},{"type":"p","text":"Correlation does not establish causation."},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"h","text":"Build a solid foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentiles"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Distributions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"p-values"},{"text":"Effect sizes"},{"text":"Statistical power"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"t-tests"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Chi-square"},{"text":"Non-parametric tests"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Later learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multiple regression"},{"text":"Factor analysis"},{"text":"Mediation/moderation"},{"text":"Reliability analysis"},{"text":"Multilevel models"},{"text":"Longitudinal analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data-analysis tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least one strong statistical workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Beginner"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SPSS/JASP"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Intermediate"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"scikit-learn"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Python Documentation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/"},{"type":"p","text":"pandas","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/"},{"type":"h","text":"Research workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw data","Cleaning","Coding","Analysis","Visualisation","Statistical interpretation","Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative research"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Codebooks"},{"text":"Reflexivity"},{"text":"Participant confidentiality"},{"text":"Qualitative validity"},{"text":"Mixed-methods research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong Research Assistant should be able to work with both qualitative and quantitative research, even if they eventually specialise in one."},{"type":"h","text":"Research ethics"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Voluntary participation"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Anonymisation"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Participant safety"},{"text":"Vulnerable populations"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"Institutional ethics review"},{"text":"Research integrity"},{"text":"Avoiding fabrication"},{"text":"Avoiding falsification"},{"text":"Avoiding plagiarism"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Psychology research involving humans requires particularly careful attention to ethics and institutional procedures."},{"type":"h","text":"Academic research skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature searching"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Systematic search concepts"},{"text":"Reference management"},{"text":"Citation styles"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Research abstracts"},{"text":"Research posters"},{"text":"Conference presentations"},{"text":"Research reports"},{"text":"Data documentation"},{"text":"Reproducibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Use tools such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Zotero"},{"text":"Google Scholar"},{"text":"PubMed"},{"text":"PsycINFO where institutionally available"},{"text":"Research databases"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"SPSS/JASP"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neuropsychology research pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"For students interested in the neuropsychology side, develop:"},{"type":"h","text":"Brain and cognition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frontal lobe"},{"text":"Temporal lobe"},{"text":"Parietal lobe"},{"text":"Occipital lobe"},{"text":"Hippocampus"},{"text":"Amygdala"},{"text":"Basal ganglia"},{"text":"Cerebellum"},{"text":"Prefrontal systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive domains"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Executive function"},{"text":"Processing speed"},{"text":"Visuospatial ability"},{"text":"Working memory"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research technologies"},{"type":"h","text":"Depending on the lab:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"Eye tracking"},{"text":"Psychophysiology"},{"text":"Behavioural experiments"},{"text":"MRI/fMRI research concepts"},{"text":"Cognitive testing"},{"text":"Computerised experiments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Undergraduate students should distinguish research exposure to neuropsychological assessment from being qualified to independently conduct clinical assessment or diagnose patients."},{"type":"h","text":"High-value projects during the BA"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Experimental Psychology Study"},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Does background music affect working-memory performance?"},{"type":"h","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hypothesis"},{"text":"Participants"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Results"},{"text":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Survey Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic stress"},{"text":"Digital behaviour"},{"text":"Sleep"},{"text":"Study habits"},{"text":"Social media use"},{"text":"Student wellbeing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Questionnaire design"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Analysis"},{"text":"Report"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use ethically appropriate procedures and avoid presenting a student project as clinical diagnosis."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Cognitive Experiment"},{"type":"h","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reaction time"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Stroop performance"},{"text":"Working memory"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a reproducible analysis notebook."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Qualitative Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct an appropriately supervised interview study and perform:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Transcription","Coding","Themes","Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Psychology Research Dashboard"},{"type":"h","text":"Create a dashboard showing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sample characteristics"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Group differences"},{"text":"Correlations"},{"text":"Trends"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Literature Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Choose a topic such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Social media and cognition"},{"text":"Sleep and memory"},{"text":"AI and mental health"},{"text":"Digital behaviour"},{"text":"Learning and attention"},{"text":"Cognitive ageing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a structured literature review with properly cited sources."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Psychology Research"},{"text":"Psychology + statistics + research methods"},{"text":"Senior Researcher"}],[{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Cognition + experiments + data"},{"text":"Cognitive Researcher"}],[{"text":"Neuropsychology Research"},{"text":"Neuroscience + cognition + assessment research"},{"text":"Neuropsychology Research Associate"}],[{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Behaviour + experimentation + data"},{"text":"Behavioural Scientist"}],[{"text":"Mental Health Research"},{"text":"Psychology + public health + research"},{"text":"Mental Health Researcher"}],[{"text":"Health Psychology"},{"text":"Psychology + health research + statistics"},{"text":"Health Research Associate"}],[{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Learning + education + research"},{"text":"Education Researcher"}],[{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Behaviour + interviews + usability + analytics"},{"text":"UX Researcher"}],[{"text":"Consumer Behaviour"},{"text":"Psychology + marketing + experiments"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Researcher"}],[{"text":"Organisational Psychology"},{"text":"Psychology + workplace research + analytics"},{"text":"People/OB Researcher"}],[{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Psychology + clinical research methods"},{"text":"Clinical Research Coordinator"}],[{"text":"AI & Human Behaviour"},{"text":"Psychology + HCI + AI"},{"text":"Human-AI Behaviour Researcher"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government / research / academic ecosystem"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation / ecosystem","Relevant exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"ICMR institutes"},{"text":"Health and behavioural research"}],[{"text":"AIIMS ecosystem"},{"text":"Clinical/health research exposure"}],[{"text":"CSIR institutes"},{"text":"Scientific/biomedical research"}],[{"text":"NIMHANS ecosystem"},{"text":"Mental health/neuroscience research"}],[{"text":"University psychology departments"},{"text":"Academic research"}],[{"text":"IIT/IISc research groups"},{"text":"Cognitive science/HCI/neuroscience research"}],[{"text":"Public-health research organisations"},{"text":"Population/mental-health studies"}],[{"text":"Government health programmes"},{"text":"Behavioural and health research"}],[{"text":"Educational research organisations"},{"text":"Learning/child development research"}],[{"text":"PM Internship Scheme"},{"text":"Where current eligibility permits"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Indian Council of Medical Research","url":"https://www.icmr.gov.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"AIIMS New Delhi","url":"https://www.aiims.edu/"},{"type":"p","text":"CSIR","url":"https://www.csir.res.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Private / research-sector internships"},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology research labs"},{"text":"Behavioural-science organisations"},{"text":"Mental-health research organisations"},{"text":"Clinical research organisations"},{"text":"Public-health organisations"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"UX research teams"},{"text":"Market research companies"},{"text":"Consumer-insights teams"},{"text":"EdTech research teams"},{"text":"HR/people analytics teams"},{"text":"AI/HCI research labs"},{"text":"Social-impact research organisations"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["one where the student performs literature review","participant/data work","analysis","research reporting, rather than only administrative tasks."],"sep":"+","label":"Best internship"}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification / learning area","Why it helps"],"rows":[[{"text":"Research Methodology"},{"text":"Core research capability"}],[{"text":"Statistics for Psychology"},{"text":"Quantitative research"}],[{"text":"SPSS/JASP"},{"text":"Psychology research analysis"}],[{"text":"R for Statistics"},{"text":"Advanced research"}],[{"text":"Python for Data Analysis"},{"text":"Research data"}],[{"text":"Qualitative Research"},{"text":"Interviews/coding"}],[{"text":"Experimental Design"},{"text":"Behavioural research"}],[{"text":"Systematic Review Methods"},{"text":"Literature research"}],[{"text":"Research Ethics"},{"text":"Human-subject research"}],[{"text":"Scientific Writing"},{"text":"Publication"}],[{"text":"Neuroscience fundamentals"},{"text":"Neuropsychology pathway"}],[{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Health/medical research"}],[{"text":"GIS/data visualisation where relevant"},{"text":"Population/environment research"}],[{"text":"AI for Research"},{"text":"Modern research workflows"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Priority rule","text":"For a Research Assistant, research experience + statistics + a strong research project + faculty/lab recommendation generally matter more than collecting unrelated certificates."}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Realistic first-job titles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Psychology Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Project Assistant"},{"text":"Research Associate — Junior"},{"text":"Behavioural Research Assistant"},{"text":"Cognitive Science Research Assistant"},{"text":"Neuropsychology Research Assistant"},{"text":"Psychological Research Assistant"},{"text":"Clinical Research Assistant"},{"text":"Clinical Research Coordinator — Junior"},{"text":"Mental Health Research Assistant"},{"text":"Public Health Research Assistant"},{"text":"Social Science Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research Data Assistant"},{"text":"Research Coordinator — Junior"},{"text":"Study Coordinator — Junior"},{"text":"Survey Research Assistant"},{"text":"Qualitative Research Assistant"},{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Research Assistant"},{"text":"Behavioural Science Assistant"},{"text":"Academic Project Assistant"},{"text":"Research Documentation Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Role-to-skill mapping"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Stack the posting asks for","Where the student proves it"],"rows":[[{"text":"Psychology Research Assistant"},{"text":"Psychology + research methods"},{"text":"Research project"}],[{"text":"Behavioural Research Assistant"},{"text":"Experimentation + statistics"},{"text":"Behavioural experiment"}],[{"text":"Cognitive Research Assistant"},{"text":"Cognition + experimental methods"},{"text":"Cognitive study"}],[{"text":"Neuropsychology RA"},{"text":"Neuroscience + cognition + research"},{"text":"Lab project"}],[{"text":"Clinical Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research + documentation"},{"text":"Clinical-research internship"}],[{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"Interviews + usability + analysis"},{"text":"UX study"}],[{"text":"Research Data Assistant"},{"text":"Statistics + Excel/R/Python"},{"text":"Analysis notebook"}],[{"text":"Qualitative RA"},{"text":"Interviews + coding"},{"text":"Qualitative research"}],[{"text":"Academic Project Assistant"},{"text":"Research + writing"},{"text":"Literature review"}],[{"text":"Mental Health Research Assistant"},{"text":"Psychology + research ethics"},{"text":"Mental-health research project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career reality"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Assistant is one of the most appropriate entry-level targets for this degree."},{"type":"p","text":"However, some university, clinical and neuroscience research positions may prefer:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Master's students"},{"text":"Specific research experience"},{"text":"Psychology/related discipline"},{"text":"Statistical skills"},{"text":"Lab experience"},{"text":"Particular software"},{"text":"Experience with human-subject research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, students should apply broadly to research internships, project assistant roles, university labs and research organisations during Years 2–4."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["PG option","Best for"],"rows":[[{"text":"MA/MSc Psychology"},{"text":"General psychology research"}],[{"text":"MSc Applied Psychology"},{"text":"Applied research"}],[{"text":"MSc Clinical Psychology"},{"text":"Clinical pathway, subject to current professional rules"}],[{"text":"MA Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Counselling/research pathway"}],[{"text":"MSc Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Cognition research"}],[{"text":"MSc Neuroscience"},{"text":"Neuroscience research"}],[{"text":"MSc Neuropsychology"},{"text":"Neuropsychology research"}],[{"text":"MSc Clinical Research"},{"text":"Health/clinical research"}],[{"text":"MPH"},{"text":"Public-health research"}],[{"text":"MSc Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Behavioural research"}],[{"text":"MSc Data Science/Statistics"},{"text":"Quantitative research"}],[{"text":"MA Research Psychology"},{"text":"Research specialisation where available"}],[{"text":"MA Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Education research"}],[{"text":"MA Organisational Psychology"},{"text":"Workplace research"}],[{"text":"PhD Psychology"},{"text":"Academic research"}],[{"text":"PhD Cognitive Science/Neuroscience"},{"text":"Advanced research"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Important professional distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"A student should not assume that a BA + research internship qualifies them to practise independently as a clinical psychologist, counsellor, or neuropsychologist."},{"type":"p","text":"Those pathways can have separate professional education, supervised-training and registration requirements. Check the current rules of the relevant Indian regulatory/professional body and institution."}]},{"heading":"Study abroad, country by country","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Example universities / ecosystem","Scholarship route","Gate to check"],"rows":[[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Stanford, University of Michigan, UC San Diego and other psychology/cognitive-science schools"},{"text":"Fulbright + university funding"},{"text":"Research profile"}],[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"UCL, King's College London, University of Edinburgh and other psychology/neuroscience programmes"},{"text":"Chevening + university funding"},{"text":"Academic prerequisites"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"University of Toronto, UBC, McGill and other research universities"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Supervisor/programme fit"}],[{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Universities with psychology, neuroscience and cognitive-science programmes"},{"text":"DAAD"},{"text":"Programme language + prerequisites"}],[{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Leiden, Amsterdam, Utrecht and other psychology/cognitive-science programmes"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Academic requirements"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"University of Melbourne, ANU and other research universities"},{"text":"Australia Awards + university funding"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}],[{"text":"Switzerland"},{"text":"University of Zurich, ETH ecosystem and other research institutions"},{"text":"Institutional funding"},{"text":"Strong academic/research profile"}],[{"text":"Japan"},{"text":"Universities with psychology, cognitive science and neuroscience research"},{"text":"MEXT"},{"text":"Academic + programme requirements"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"USIEF / Fulbright-Nehru","url":"https://www.usief.org.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"DAAD India","url":"https://www.daad.in/en/"},{"type":"h","text":"Application portfolio"},{"type":"h","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong GPA"},{"text":"Research experience"},{"text":"Research assistantship"},{"text":"Dissertation/project"},{"text":"Statistical skills"},{"text":"Research paper/poster"},{"text":"Academic CV"},{"text":"Strong recommendation letters"},{"text":"Statement of Purpose"},{"text":"Research proposal where required"},{"text":"English-language test if required"},{"text":"Evidence of relevant lab methods"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For research-heavy Master's/PhD programmes, research experience and supervisor fit can be more important than generic certificates."}]},{"heading":"Going forward","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Student","Research Intern","Research Assistant","Research Associate","Senior Research Associate","Research Scientist/Researcher","Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA/MSc","Research Assistant","PhD","Postdoctoral Researcher","Faculty/Research Scientist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical/health research route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","Psychology/Clinical Research PG","Research Assistant","Study Coordinator","Research Associate","Clinical Research Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Behavioural-science route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","Behavioural Research Intern","Research Assistant","Behavioural Research Associate","Behavioural Scientist","Senior Behavioural Scientist"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD routes"},{"type":"h","text":"Possible doctoral directions include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Cognitive Psychology"},{"text":"Clinical Psychology"},{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Neuropsychology"},{"text":"Cognitive Neuroscience"},{"text":"Neuroscience"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Social Psychology"},{"text":"Developmental Psychology"},{"text":"Health Psychology"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Organisational Psychology"},{"text":"Experimental Psychology"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Mental Health Research"},{"text":"Computational Psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Research careers will increasingly combine psychology with computational methods, large datasets, digital behavioural measurement, neuroscience, AI and human-computer interaction."},{"type":"h","text":"AI can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature discovery"},{"text":"Document screening"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Coding assistance"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Qualitative coding support"},{"text":"Statistical programming"},{"text":"Research documentation"},{"text":"Research synthesis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But researchers remain responsible for methodological validity, ethics, interpretation, reproducibility and scientific integrity."},{"type":"h","text":"A particularly strong future profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Psychology","Research Methods","Statistics","Experimental Design","Data Science","Neuroscience/Behavioural Science","AI"],"sep":"+"}]}]}